From: HyprTomic maintenance <noreply@example.invalid>
Subject: [PATCH] pipewire: defer destruction out of the "destroying" emission

quickshell segfaults (SIGSEGV) whenever a tracked PipeWire object that is
the current default sink is removed (e.g. Sunshine's virtual
"sink-sunshine-stereo" sink is unloaded when the host stops streaming, a
Bluetooth/USB audio device disconnects, ...).

Crash report log tail:

    Unbinding object PwNode(0x..., id=<n>/bound)
    Destroying object PwNode(0x..., id=<n>/unbound)
    INFO quickshell.service.pipewire.defaults: Default configured sink destroyed.

Stack: PwBindableObject::safeDestroy() -> emit destroying() ->
PwObjectIface::onObjectDestroying() (`delete this`) and the defaults
tracker handlers run inside the same emission; any QML endpoint invoked in
that window (bindings on Pipewire.defaultAudioSink, Pipewire.nodes model
consumers, ...) is evaluated while QML state is already being freed and
crashes in QV4 (lookupSingletonProperty / memcpy).

Fix: never delete either object from inside the signal emission. Both the
QML-facing interface and the pipewire object are removed on the next event
loop turn instead, so the emission (and the QML side effects it triggers)
complete with live objects.

--- a/src/services/pipewire/qml.cpp
+++ b/src/services/pipewire/qml.cpp
@@ -25,7 +25,7 @@ PwObjectIface::PwObjectIface(PwBindableObject* object): QObject(object), object(
 	QObject::connect(object, &PwBindableObject::destroying, this, &PwObjectIface::onObjectDestroying);
 }
 
-void PwObjectIface::onObjectDestroying() { delete this; }
+void PwObjectIface::onObjectDestroying() { this->deleteLater(); }
 
 void PwObjectIface::ref() {
 	this->refcount++;
--- a/src/services/pipewire/registry.cpp
+++ b/src/services/pipewire/registry.cpp
@@ -46,7 +46,9 @@ void PwBindableObject::safeDestroy() {
 	qCDebug(logRegistry) << "Destroying object" << this;
 	emit this->destroying(this);
 	this->id = 0;
-	delete this;
+	// quickshell patch: defer deletion so QML endpoints invoked during the
+	// destroying emission cannot touch freed state (segfault workaround).
+	this->deleteLater();
 }
 
 void PwBindableObject::debugId(QDebug& debug) const {
